.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt LOONGARCH_SYSCON 4 loongarch64
.Os
.\" .Nm loongarch64/loongarch_syscon
.Sh NAME
.Nm loongarch_syscon
.Nd LoongArch flattened device tree system controller
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in the
kernel configuration file:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Cd "options FDT"
.Cd "device syscon"
.Cd "device loongarch_syscon"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver exposes memory-mapped system controller registers to kernel
clients through the system controller interface.
It attaches to enabled flattened device tree nodes with the compatible
string
.Qq syscon
and uses the register range described by the device tree.
.Pp
The driver attaches early so that other device tree drivers can obtain
access to system controller registers during initialization.
It does not provide a user-visible device node and does not enumerate
ACPI devices.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fdt 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver was added in the LoongArch port of
.Fx 16.0 .
